# OSCP IMU ROS2 Driver (oscp_imu_ros2)

A configurable ROS 2 IMU driver supporting multiple output formats including raw IMU data, quaternion, Euler angles, rotation matrix, and standard ROS `sensor_msgs/Imu`.

---

## Installation

Clone and build inside your ROS 2 workspace:

Clone inside your ROS 2 workspace:

```bash
cd ~/ros2_ws/src

git clone https://github.com/yourusername/oscp_imu_ros2.git

```
Install dependencies

```bash
cd ..

rosdep update

rosdep install --from-paths src -y --ignore-src --rosdistro $ROS_DISTRO

```
Build and source workspace 

```bash

colcon build --packages-up-to oscp_imu_ros2 --symlink-install

source install/setup.bash
```
---

## Usage

Launch the IMU node using yaml configurations:

```bash
ros2 launch oscp_imu_ros2 oscp_imu.launch.py config_file:=test.yaml
```

---

## Launch Configuration

### Core Device Settings

- device (default: `/dev/ttyUSB0`)
  Serial port used by the IMU

- baudrate (default: `921600`)
  Serial communication speed

- frame_id (default: `imu_link`)
  TF frame used in published messages

---

### Config File

- config_file (default: `imu_test_preset.yaml`)
  Located in `oscp_imu_ros2/config/`

---

### Output Flags

- pub_accel_in_g (default: false)
- oscp_raw_enabled (default: true)
- oscp_quat_enabled (default: true)
- oscp_euler_enabled (default: true)
- oscp_rotation_matrix_enabled (default: true)
- standard_ros_enabled (default: true)

---

## Topics

### Raw Outputs
- /oscp/raw
- /oscp/quat
- /oscp/euler
- /oscp/rot

### ROS Standard
- /oscp/imu/data (sensor_msgs/Imu)
- /ocsp/imu/mag (sensor_msgs/Mag)
- /oscp/imu/temp (sensor_msgs/Temp)

---

## Features

- Multi-format IMU output
- ROS 2 native integration
- Configurable runtime parameters
- Lightweight serial driver
- Supports multiple IMU telemetry modes

